{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1559840-deivents-consparicy-rules-for-general-cofd","id":1559840,"title":"Deivents Consparicy rules for General CofD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-08T12:53:46-07:00","id":1559840,"title":"Deivents Consparicy rules for General CofD","content":"Would Deivents Consparicy rules need to be Modified for them to work as Hunters in other games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T14:32:23-07:00","id":1559843,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by &quot;as Hunters&quot; in other games? There are approaches to the concept of &quot;Hunter&quot; where you either don't need special rules, or Vigil would be more than enough, and ones where Conspiracies might do more as a mechanical framework for antagonists. If your players have run afoul of a small group of individual Hunters (regardless of whether or not they're part of a larger group) and those specific individuals are meant to be significant and lasting parts of the game? Conspiracies probably aren't going to help much there; those rules are too abstracted to really capture getting hounded by Mulder and Scully despite them being FBI agents with a whole government agency behind them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T16:29:11-07:00","id":1559845,"title":"","content":"Repersneting of a Hunter Cell, Compact, or Conpsacy. <br /> <br /> <br /> It makes organizing what to do with the hunters easier in my eyes, but I am unsure if any changes need to happen...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T17:31:24-07:00","id":1559847,"title":"","content":"Well, Vigil Hunters are designed to be the protagonists of their own game, not the antagonist of the other game-lines. Unless you're running a game where actively dismantling a Compact or Conspiracy is important to the plot (Cells are too small to really make it worth it), interfacing with the specific Hunters is still going to be the focus of what's going on.<br /> <br /> Your average vampire that's being targeted by Network Zero is unlikely to really see them as an organized threat that needs to be dismantled (and if they do, they might not want to get rid of them if they can be pointed at other supernaturals instead). A bunch of humans that find out the vampires are real and try to warn the herd about them? That's why Princes organize enough power to create a Masquerade so the majority of people react with disbelief while vampires can use mind-control powers to discredit those with evidence, and stealth powers to get rid of the evidence. It's not something where you're going to get into the whole mechanical system because vampires default to, &quot;we'll be alive in 100 years, these idiots will be dead in a few decades,&quot; when considering what to do with the latest group of humans trying to make a fuss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-09T15:20:00-07:00","id":1559857,"title":"","content":"Network Zero could also invoke Conditions like Notoriety or the cutting of Merits, making a Haven turn form <br /> <br /> And I would say Standing 1-3 Conpsecies would be perfect for cells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-09T16:00:27-07:00","id":1559858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1559840-deivents-consparicy-rules-for-general-cofd?p=1559857#post1559857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I would say Standing 1-3 Conpsecies would be perfect for cells.</div> </div> </div> </div>A cell has headcounts in the low double-digits at most. Any conspiracy has the nominal capacity to engage in conspiracy actions (with the unmodified Send Agents metrics being up to four Baselines with fairly expensive equipment and up to however many Devoted are attached to the originating Node), and, as the most ground-level protagonist-facing version of the organization mechanics, Geist's krewes need to be built deliberately flimsy and just starting out to not have at least as many extra characters as Hunter 1e attributes to a single cell. &quot;Locally influential or regional but diffuse&quot; is pretty much an exact fit for the scope of most compacts as Hunter describes them.<br /> <br /> Black Vans on the Storyteller's Vault has tips for modeling hunters and other supernatural beings as deviants and using the conspiracy mechanics to model different types of plot structure enforcement, but most gamelines that aren't Deviant don't have a core gameplay loop that requires tracking the big-picture goals and maneuvers of one or more conspiracies that are at least entrenched enough to have a hand on the steering wheel in whatever population center your game takes place in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-09T16:35:55-07:00","id":1559859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1559840-deivents-consparicy-rules-for-general-cofd?p=1559857#post1559857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I would say Standing 1-3 Conpsecies would be perfect for cells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Standing 1-2 is described in Deviant as &quot;locally influential or regional but diffuse&quot; organizations. This is the level of particularly well equipped compacts. (Any Deviant conspiracy is assumed to have the means to feasibly pursue, harry, and capture or eliminate the Remade. Network Zero is a community of cryptozoologists with cameras. Just being a &quot;locally influential or regional but diffuse&quot; organization alone doesn't make you a conspiracy. At best, if you used Deviant conspiracy rules to model Network Zero, you would have to do so keeping in mind that there are many conspiracy actions that are simply outside the scope of what they are equipped to do.)<br /> <br /> Cells are like five guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-10T01:34:07-07:00","id":1559867,"title":"","content":"I wonder about using the Deviant system to maybe try mapping out Hunter C&amp;Cs without actually engaging the whole mechanic.<br /> <br /> Like I personally like creating NPC character sheets, not because I intend to roll any dice, but because it gives me a better picture of the NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-21T12:57:42-07:00","id":1560143,"title":"","content":"From what I understand, the next STV supplement for Deviant (&quot;Deep Dive&quot;, a Night Horrors style book based on conspiracies) is planned to have a section in it that will go more in depth on modeling conspiracy-like entities from other gamelines as Deviant-style conspiracies. <br /> <br /> I agree that even the smallest conspiracy is too big to represent a Hunter cell; though it might work for something larger than a Hunter cell but smaller than a Hunter compact, such as a werewolf Pack or a small Sin-Eater Krewe. It could also be used to represent other local organizations from the various gamelines that include supernaturals of that type and mortals adjacent to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T15:46:58-07:00","id":1561255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1559840-deivents-consparicy-rules-for-general-cofd#post1559840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Deivents Consparicy rules need to be Modified for them to work as Hunters in other games?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best way to sum up what everyone is trying to say is:<br /> <br /> Deviant Conspiracy rules model conspiracies. This is not a size or type of organization, it's an <b><i>activity/theme</i></b>.<br /> <br /> And that's what runs afoul of what you're describing, because Hunting is <i>another</i> activity and theme.<br /> <br /> The same group of people can do both, hunt and conspire, but the rules will take care of the later.<br /> <br /> When the point of those hunters in the game is to investigate the characters and meet them at times face to face, sometimes leveraging their resources and connections as individuals with the sole purpose of finishing off the monsters, Conspiracy rules won't help you no matter what organization the hunters form, even an actual Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> But if you want to run a conspiracy heavy game a l\u00e1 Deviant, where you need to model the organization as a whole and pit its entirety against the PCs, then sure. But what type of game is this?<br /> <br /> Deviant assumes Conspiracies keep track of them and want to get them so badly they'll never be left alone. The premise is there even a single Chronicle will see the downfall of more than one Conspiracy and that they matter as a whole rather than just as sources of characters to use. And Deviants are particular targets as they have no actual society to shield them like most others do.<br /> <br /> You can run a similar game with any splat with few adjustments, but that's not about hunters. You can also run a conspiracy game where the players have their own Conspiracy, that could be interesting. You have to keep in mind also that other splats usually have whole societies not to Conspiracies, but to their whole Web. If a Conspiracy starts to bring institutional weight to the fight, they will stir their supernatural cousins that can usually turn the game against them quite effectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}